1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,530
Max needs comfortable school shoes.

2
00:00:02,680 --> 00:00:06,280
One useful pair. No enormous fruit this time.

3
00:00:06,430 --> 00:00:08,710
Can shoes be too ripe?

4
00:00:08,860 --> 00:00:13,340
Only if they start smelling like bananas.
Let's try feet.

5
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:17,090
How should they feel?

6
00:00:17,240 --> 00:00:20,840
Comfortable. My toes would like a little
space.

7
00:00:20,990 --> 00:00:23,270
They live there all day.

8
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:27,460
Mine would like room to move at recess, too.

9
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:32,970
One pair, comfortable fit, forty-dollar
budget.

10
00:00:33,120 --> 00:00:35,840
Three checks. I can share those.

11
00:00:35,990 --> 00:00:39,590
What goes at the top of the list?

12
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:43,780
Fit first. Max has to wear them all day.

13
00:00:45,250 --> 00:00:47,229
Do these feel tight?

14
00:00:47,379 --> 00:00:49,831
A little at the front.

15
00:00:49,981 --> 00:00:53,852
We will measure both feet at the store.

16
00:00:54,002 --> 00:00:57,400
Both? My toes aren't arguing about it.

17
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:01,282
Everyone ready?

18
00:01:01,432 --> 00:01:03,411
All six of us.

19
00:01:03,561 --> 00:01:07,432
And twelve feet. I checked the easy way.

20
00:01:07,582 --> 00:01:12,400
Thanks, Max. I'll count the people and trust
your feet.

21
00:01:15,250 --> 00:01:18,146
Is the list facing the right way?

22
00:01:18,296 --> 00:01:21,998
It will when I open it. An improvement
already.

23
00:01:22,148 --> 00:01:25,851
Can I take a look when you open it?

24
00:01:26,001 --> 00:01:29,300
Please do. Two sets of eyes this time.

25
00:01:30,250 --> 00:01:32,530
Tell us if anything pinches.

26
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:36,280
We have time to find the right fit.

27
00:01:36,430 --> 00:01:38,710
My toes appreciate the schedule.

28
00:01:38,860 --> 00:01:43,340
You get to tell us when a pair feels right.

29
00:01:45,250 --> 00:01:48,410
Shoes first, sensible questions along the way.

30
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:50,400
We have a plan.

31
00:01:50,550 --> 00:01:53,270
And our feet are coming too.

32
00:01:53,420 --> 00:01:58,340
Lucky for us. They know how to get to the
door.

33
00:02:00,250 --> 00:02:03,410
The shoe store is on this floor.

34
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:06,280
Excellent. Our feet can start locally.

35
00:02:06,430 --> 00:02:09,150
Which way does the directory point?

36
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:12,460
Along this floor. No stairs for us.

37
00:02:15,250 --> 00:02:17,970
A moving staircase. Very ambitious stairs.

38
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:19,960
That is the escalator.

39
00:02:20,110 --> 00:02:23,710
Our stairs at home are taking a break.

40
00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:28,340
Saves them a trip. We're staying on this floor
anyway.

41
00:02:30,250 --> 00:02:32,607
The elevator is over there.

42
00:02:32,757 --> 00:02:35,568
And the store is over here.

43
00:02:35,718 --> 00:02:37,620
Then upstairs can wait.

44
00:02:37,770 --> 00:02:42,400
Good. I'd rather try shoes than ride past the
store.

45
00:02:45,250 --> 00:02:49,290
I will keep a map for the return trip.

46
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:52,600
Can it show where my feet are?

47
00:02:52,750 --> 00:02:55,470
First we find where we are.

48
00:02:55,620 --> 00:02:59,220
I know that part. They're right under me.

49
00:03:00,250 --> 00:03:03,650
Entrance behind us, shoe store to our right.

50
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:06,784
The map and the mall agree. Promising.

51
00:03:06,934 --> 00:03:09,919
Look at the sign beside the door.

52
00:03:10,069 --> 00:03:14,300
That's our shop. We can put the map away soon.

53
00:03:15,250 --> 00:03:18,757
There are shelves, a mirror, and a bench.

54
00:03:18,907 --> 00:03:21,557
A small waiting room for feet.

55
00:03:21,707 --> 00:03:25,643
And somewhere to sit while we try a pair.

56
00:03:25,793 --> 00:03:29,300
I hope the bench comes in my size.

57
00:03:30,250 --> 00:03:32,152
Let us start here.

58
00:03:32,302 --> 00:03:35,568
Comfortable bench. The shoes have strong
competition.

59
00:03:35,718 --> 00:03:38,984
Can my feet try the bench first?

60
00:03:39,134 --> 00:03:42,400
Yes. They get the first turn today.

61
00:03:45,250 --> 00:03:47,970
That box says adult size ten.

62
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:50,840
Then it is definitely not Max's.

63
00:03:50,990 --> 00:03:53,710
Who's doing the shopping today, then?

64
00:03:53,860 --> 00:03:57,900
Max is. My feet can stay in my shoes.

65
00:04:00,250 --> 00:04:03,516
Two boxes. I can manage two boxes.

66
00:04:03,666 --> 00:04:06,023
Remember the two shopping lists?

67
00:04:06,173 --> 00:04:08,074
A useful historical warning.

68
00:04:08,224 --> 00:04:12,400
Please remember which feet came with me today,
Dad.

69
00:04:15,250 --> 00:04:17,900
This may be a little snug.

70
00:04:18,050 --> 00:04:20,700
Your foot needs its own building.

71
00:04:20,850 --> 00:04:24,357
Check the box before the joke becomes work.

72
00:04:24,507 --> 00:04:29,300
I can tell without trying. That one's smaller
than your sock.

73
00:04:30,250 --> 00:04:33,850
We will not force a foot into anything.

74
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:37,600
Agreed. No shoes were harmed by my confidence.

75
00:04:37,750 --> 00:04:40,470
Whose foot are we measuring today?

76
00:04:40,620 --> 00:04:43,780
Max's. My foot is officially off duty.

77
00:04:45,250 --> 00:04:47,702
First, find the measuring station.

78
00:04:47,852 --> 00:04:51,250
Then find shoes for my actual feet.

79
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:52,906
A sensible order.

80
00:04:53,056 --> 00:04:57,400
Come on, Dad. They're both right here with me.

81
00:05:00,250 --> 00:05:03,410
The fitting room must be that way.

82
00:05:03,560 --> 00:05:05,840
Is that map upside down?

83
00:05:05,990 --> 00:05:09,150
I may have rotated the whole mall.

84
00:05:09,300 --> 00:05:13,340
Turn the paper first. It's lighter than the
building.

85
00:05:15,250 --> 00:05:17,152
We will check together.

86
00:05:17,302 --> 00:05:19,658
Nobody follows a guess alone.

87
00:05:19,808 --> 00:05:22,620
My feet vote for the group.

88
00:05:22,770 --> 00:05:27,400
I'll keep the real signs in sight while you
check.

89
00:05:30,250 --> 00:05:32,090
The arrow points here.

90
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:35,400
But the shoe store is behind us.

91
00:05:35,550 --> 00:05:37,390
That is worth checking.

92
00:05:37,540 --> 00:05:42,460
A sign behind us beats a guess in front of us.

93
00:05:45,250 --> 00:05:49,614
Shoes often have a fitting area, not a
changing room.

94
00:05:49,764 --> 00:05:52,843
I asked my map the wrong question.

95
00:05:52,993 --> 00:05:55,214
What should we ask instead?

96
00:05:55,364 --> 00:05:59,300
Where they measure feet and let us try shoes.

97
00:06:00,250 --> 00:06:02,530
Rose! What a lovely surprise.

98
00:06:02,680 --> 00:06:05,840
Hi, everyone. What are we looking for?

99
00:06:05,990 --> 00:06:07,390
Better directions, apparently.

100
00:06:07,540 --> 00:06:12,460
Directions I can help with. What were you
trying to find?

101
00:06:15,250 --> 00:06:19,290
Where is the fitting area in the shoe store?

102
00:06:19,440 --> 00:06:21,720
Which entrance did you use?

103
00:06:21,870 --> 00:06:24,590
The glass doors beside the directory.

104
00:06:24,740 --> 00:06:29,220
We came from there. Which side should we be
on?

105
00:06:30,250 --> 00:06:32,530
This end matches the entrance.

106
00:06:32,680 --> 00:06:36,280
The mall has returned to its original
position.

107
00:06:36,430 --> 00:06:38,270
Very considerate of it.

108
00:06:38,420 --> 00:06:42,460
It's easier when the doors on both match, Dad.

109
00:06:45,250 --> 00:06:48,850
I noticed a measuring device beside the bench.

110
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:49,960
Our bench!

111
00:06:50,110 --> 00:06:53,270
Then we can ask about measuring there.

112
00:06:53,420 --> 00:06:57,900
So we were closer than that map made us think.

113
00:07:00,250 --> 00:07:02,090
School shoes for Max.

114
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:04,520
Not for Dad's enormous feet.

115
00:07:04,670 --> 00:07:08,270
Then the smallest customer gets the biggest
say.

116
00:07:08,420 --> 00:07:12,460
Good. Mine have plenty to say about school
shoes.

117
00:07:15,250 --> 00:07:18,298
Enjoy the fitting. See you soon.

118
00:07:18,448 --> 00:07:19,524
Thanks, Rose.

119
00:07:19,674 --> 00:07:23,216
We will check the actual feet next.

120
00:07:23,366 --> 00:07:27,400
Give those toes a vote for me, Max.

121
00:07:30,250 --> 00:07:33,410
Same floor, back to the shoe store.

122
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:36,280
Now the map matches the place.

123
00:07:36,430 --> 00:07:39,150
And the question matches the job.

124
00:07:39,300 --> 00:07:43,340
This time I'll ask somebody who works with
feet.

125
00:07:45,250 --> 00:07:47,530
The bench waited for us.

126
00:07:47,680 --> 00:07:51,280
Very patient furniture. Let us be patient too.

127
00:07:51,430 --> 00:07:54,590
Max, do you want to start here?

128
00:07:54,740 --> 00:07:59,220
Yes. My feet have been looking forward to that
bench.

129
00:08:00,250 --> 00:08:03,410
Could you help us measure both feet?

130
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:07,160
Certainly. Please keep him seated while we
begin.

131
00:08:07,310 --> 00:08:09,150
We can do that.

132
00:08:09,300 --> 00:08:13,340
I'll sit still. My toes might have questions,
though.

133
00:08:15,250 --> 00:08:17,312
Their first break today.

134
00:08:17,462 --> 00:08:20,017
We will keep them together.

135
00:08:20,167 --> 00:08:22,722
And out of the walkway.

136
00:08:22,872 --> 00:08:27,400
My old shoes can watch. They've done enough
walking.

137
00:08:30,250 --> 00:08:34,730
Start with a children's size two, then check
the fit.

138
00:08:34,880 --> 00:08:37,600
Measurement first. My toes approve too.

139
00:08:37,750 --> 00:08:40,030
What do you think, Max?

140
00:08:40,180 --> 00:08:43,780
I want to see how the twos feel.

141
00:08:45,250 --> 00:08:47,970
Do you like this navy pair?

142
00:08:48,120 --> 00:08:51,720
Yes. The green tabs can be tiny flags.

143
00:08:51,870 --> 00:08:54,150
Comfort still gets a vote.

144
00:08:54,300 --> 00:08:58,780
My toes can tell us once both shoes are on.

145
00:09:00,250 --> 00:09:02,607
This one is size one.

146
00:09:02,757 --> 00:09:06,023
Then we should say so before trying.

147
00:09:06,173 --> 00:09:08,529
My feet like honest introductions.

148
00:09:08,679 --> 00:09:12,400
Good. I'll wait for the customer's actual
opinion.

149
00:09:15,250 --> 00:09:17,152
My toes feel squeezed.

150
00:09:17,302 --> 00:09:18,749
Then we stop.

151
00:09:18,899 --> 00:09:23,074
You do not have to get used to pain.

152
00:09:23,224 --> 00:09:27,400
Thanks. That's exactly the part I'd like to
skip.

153
00:09:30,250 --> 00:09:32,702
Thank you for telling us.

154
00:09:32,852 --> 00:09:36,250
My toes sent a very short message.

155
00:09:36,400 --> 00:09:37,432
We listened.

156
00:09:37,582 --> 00:09:42,400
Let's remember that feeling when we compare
the next size.

157
00:09:45,250 --> 00:09:48,410
We measured two. Three may be loose.

158
00:09:48,560 --> 00:09:52,160
A comparison, then back to the measured size.

159
00:09:52,310 --> 00:09:56,350
Should we call it right before he tries it?

160
00:09:56,500 --> 00:09:59,220
Let's hear from Max's heel first.

161
00:10:00,250 --> 00:10:02,312
My heel is sliding.

162
00:10:02,462 --> 00:10:04,031
Too much room?

163
00:10:04,181 --> 00:10:07,229
Yes. Loose is different from comfortable.

164
00:10:07,379 --> 00:10:12,400
I can feel it every time I lift my heel.

165
00:10:15,250 --> 00:10:19,290
Not tight, not swimming. We need a good fit.

166
00:10:19,440 --> 00:10:21,720
My feet are not boats.

167
00:10:21,870 --> 00:10:24,590
What should your heel do instead?

168
00:10:24,740 --> 00:10:28,340
Stay with me when I take a step.

169
00:10:30,250 --> 00:10:32,607
Here is the size two.

170
00:10:32,757 --> 00:10:35,113
Same model, correct starting size.

171
00:10:35,263 --> 00:10:38,074
Now we check how it feels.

172
00:10:38,224 --> 00:10:42,400
The number matches. My toes get the final say.

173
00:10:45,250 --> 00:10:48,410
No pushing. Tell me if anything pinches.

174
00:10:48,560 --> 00:10:51,720
So far, my toes are staying cheerful.

175
00:10:51,870 --> 00:10:54,150
What about the other side?

176
00:10:54,300 --> 00:10:58,340
Give me a second. I want to feel both.

177
00:11:00,250 --> 00:11:02,805
I can wiggle my toes.

178
00:11:02,955 --> 00:11:05,017
An important school subject.

179
00:11:05,167 --> 00:11:07,722
And the heel feels secure?

180
00:11:07,872 --> 00:11:12,400
Yes. It stays put when I move my foot.

181
00:11:15,250 --> 00:11:18,061
How does the left one feel?

182
00:11:18,211 --> 00:11:20,568
Comfortable. The right one too.

183
00:11:20,718 --> 00:11:22,165
Two useful answers.

184
00:11:22,315 --> 00:11:27,400
And I'll take those answers over a number on a
box.

185
00:11:30,250 --> 00:11:32,819
Stand naturally. No need to pose.

186
00:11:32,969 --> 00:11:36,369
The shoes are applying for an everyday job.

187
00:11:36,519 --> 00:11:40,334
Even on a day when I run at recess?

188
00:11:40,484 --> 00:11:44,300
That's why we want to see you stand normally.

189
00:11:45,250 --> 00:11:47,229
No pinching. No sliding.

190
00:11:47,379 --> 00:11:49,831
And no dramatic shoe escape.

191
00:11:49,981 --> 00:11:52,432
How does the sole feel?

192
00:11:52,582 --> 00:11:57,400
Steady. I can feel the floor without a hard
edge.

193
00:12:00,250 --> 00:12:01,819
They look good.

194
00:12:01,969 --> 00:12:03,538
And feel good?

195
00:12:03,688 --> 00:12:07,229
Yes. My feet agree with the mirror.

196
00:12:07,379 --> 00:12:12,400
The mirror doesn't get to make the choice for
you.

197
00:12:15,250 --> 00:12:20,043
There is room at the toes and support at the
heel.

198
00:12:20,193 --> 00:12:24,129
The size is a clue, not the whole answer.

199
00:12:24,279 --> 00:12:26,929
My heel stays with me now.

200
00:12:27,079 --> 00:12:29,300
Good. Trust your feet first.

201
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:32,970
Is thirty-two dollars the full price?

202
00:12:33,120 --> 00:12:34,520
Yes, including tax.

203
00:12:34,670 --> 00:12:37,830
That leaves eight dollars in our budget.

204
00:12:37,980 --> 00:12:42,460
And I can wear them to school without sore
toes.

205
00:12:45,250 --> 00:12:48,850
A giant shoe would hold the shopping list.

206
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:52,160
We need shoes for Max, not luggage.

207
00:12:52,310 --> 00:12:54,590
My feet have already voted.

208
00:12:54,740 --> 00:12:59,220
Fair enough. The list doesn't need a pair of
shoes.

209
00:13:00,250 --> 00:13:04,186
We will keep the new pair boxed for school.

210
00:13:04,336 --> 00:13:07,414
They can rest before their first day.

211
00:13:07,564 --> 00:13:10,214
What will you walk home in?

212
00:13:10,364 --> 00:13:14,300
My own green ones. I know how those feel.

213
00:13:15,250 --> 00:13:17,970
The familiar pair gets us home.

214
00:13:18,120 --> 00:13:22,160
They know the route. Better than our first
map.

215
00:13:22,310 --> 00:13:25,470
Which pair is in the box then?

216
00:13:25,620 --> 00:13:29,220
The navy pair, saving its steps for school.

217
00:13:30,250 --> 00:13:33,850
Two shoes, both size two, one matching box.

218
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:36,280
My most successful box inspection.

219
00:13:36,430 --> 00:13:40,470
Matching green tabs, too. That's the pair Max
chose.

220
00:13:40,620 --> 00:13:43,340
Good. Let's keep those two together.

221
00:13:45,250 --> 00:13:46,697
Nothing left behind.

222
00:13:46,847 --> 00:13:50,113
Except the shoes that did not fit.

223
00:13:50,263 --> 00:13:52,620
Those stay with the store.

224
00:13:52,770 --> 00:13:57,400
And our one good pair stays together in its
box.

225
00:14:00,250 --> 00:14:03,410
This navy pair in children's size two?

226
00:14:03,560 --> 00:14:04,520
Yes, please.

227
00:14:04,670 --> 00:14:06,070
The comfortable one.

228
00:14:06,220 --> 00:14:09,820
That's the size we checked on both shoes.

229
00:14:09,970 --> 00:14:13,130
And it's the one my heel liked.

230
00:14:15,250 --> 00:14:16,650
Both shoes match.

231
00:14:16,800 --> 00:14:18,640
And both feet approved.

232
00:14:18,790 --> 00:14:19,750
Excellent references.

233
00:14:19,900 --> 00:14:23,940
You can ask my heels. They finally stayed put.

234
00:14:24,090 --> 00:14:27,690
Then we can put this pair through checkout.

235
00:14:30,250 --> 00:14:31,756
Thirty-two dollars total.

236
00:14:31,906 --> 00:14:36,723
Two twenties make forty. This number gets a
second check.

237
00:14:36,873 --> 00:14:39,325
How much should come back?

238
00:14:39,475 --> 00:14:42,400
Eight dollars, if our total's right.

239
00:14:45,250 --> 00:14:47,152
Here is forty dollars.

240
00:14:47,302 --> 00:14:51,477
The shoes are going to school, not the money.

241
00:14:51,627 --> 00:14:53,529
The money stays here.

242
00:14:53,679 --> 00:14:57,400
Only thirty-two stays, Dad. The rest comes
back.

243
00:15:00,250 --> 00:15:03,175
Eight dollars change and your receipt.

244
00:15:03,325 --> 00:15:05,777
Forty minus thirty-two is eight.

245
00:15:05,927 --> 00:15:07,906
No shirt change needed.

246
00:15:08,056 --> 00:15:12,400
I'll take this kind of change any day, Max.

247
00:15:15,250 --> 00:15:17,970
We stayed eight dollars under budget.

248
00:15:18,120 --> 00:15:20,400
And received eight dollars change.

249
00:15:20,550 --> 00:15:22,830
Same amount, two different reasons.

250
00:15:22,980 --> 00:15:27,460
Right. One starts with our limit, one with the
bills.

251
00:15:30,250 --> 00:15:33,410
The receipt proves which pair we bought.

252
00:15:33,560 --> 00:15:35,840
My toes could testify too.

253
00:15:35,990 --> 00:15:38,710
The paper is easier to file.

254
00:15:38,860 --> 00:15:42,460
And the paper actually fits in Dad's wallet.

255
00:15:45,250 --> 00:15:48,410
What if we need to return them?

256
00:15:48,560 --> 00:15:51,720
Unworn, with the receipt, within fourteen
days.

257
00:15:51,870 --> 00:15:54,150
We will keep everything together.

258
00:15:54,300 --> 00:15:58,340
Good. We know exactly which box goes with
them.

259
00:16:00,250 --> 00:16:02,530
Is a refund more change?

260
00:16:02,680 --> 00:16:06,280
It is money returned after an accepted return.

261
00:16:06,430 --> 00:16:09,590
Today we are keeping our comfortable pair.

262
00:16:09,740 --> 00:16:13,340
Then my toes can skip the paperwork today.

263
00:16:15,250 --> 00:16:17,530
Here you are. Thank you.

264
00:16:17,680 --> 00:16:19,960
Thank you for your help.

265
00:16:20,110 --> 00:16:23,270
The right pair found the right family.

266
00:16:23,420 --> 00:16:28,340
One box is just right. Thank you for listening
to Max.

267
00:16:30,250 --> 00:16:33,516
Six people, one pair of new shoes.

268
00:16:33,666 --> 00:16:36,023
Twelve feet, still accounted for.

269
00:16:36,173 --> 00:16:37,620
A complete inventory.

270
00:16:37,770 --> 00:16:42,400
And the new ones are riding home in their box.

271
00:16:45,250 --> 00:16:47,090
One box, not two?

272
00:16:47,240 --> 00:16:49,520
One matching pair. We checked.

273
00:16:49,670 --> 00:16:52,830
Then let us check the way home.

274
00:16:52,980 --> 00:16:57,460
This time can we ask before the mall turns
around?

275
00:17:00,250 --> 00:17:03,516
Entrance this way. Does the map agree?

276
00:17:03,666 --> 00:17:06,477
Yes, and so do the doors.

277
00:17:06,627 --> 00:17:08,074
A strong majority.

278
00:17:08,224 --> 00:17:12,400
After that detour, I'm happy to take a vote.

279
00:17:15,250 --> 00:17:17,970
Are we trying the moving stairs?

280
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:21,720
We do not need to go upstairs today.

281
00:17:21,870 --> 00:17:24,590
The straight path takes us home.

282
00:17:24,740 --> 00:17:28,780
Good. My old shoes know how to go straight.

283
00:17:30,250 --> 00:17:32,530
I checked before I guessed.

284
00:17:32,680 --> 00:17:34,960
And we got here together.

285
00:17:35,110 --> 00:17:38,270
The mall did not need rotating again.

286
00:17:38,420 --> 00:17:42,900
It's easier when the doors stay on the same
side.

287
00:17:45,250 --> 00:17:47,530
How do your feet feel?

288
00:17:47,680 --> 00:17:52,160
Ready for home. And ready for the new pair
later.

289
00:17:52,310 --> 00:17:54,590
Shall we head out together?

290
00:17:54,740 --> 00:17:57,900
Yes, and the boxed pair comes too.

291
00:18:00,250 --> 00:18:02,607
Home with the correct box.

292
00:18:02,757 --> 00:18:04,658
And considerably better directions.

293
00:18:04,808 --> 00:18:07,620
My feet enjoyed the second plan.

294
00:18:07,770 --> 00:18:12,400
I think the box had the easiest walk of all.

295
00:18:15,250 --> 00:18:19,290
Let us keep shoes away from the kitchen
worktop.

296
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:21,280
Right place, right purpose.

297
00:18:21,430 --> 00:18:23,710
Another map we can understand.

298
00:18:23,860 --> 00:18:28,340
The bench near the door suits this box just
fine.

299
00:18:30,250 --> 00:18:34,290
The receipt stays safe while the shoes stay
clean.

300
00:18:34,440 --> 00:18:36,720
Now we can find both.

301
00:18:36,870 --> 00:18:38,270
No upside-down filing.

302
00:18:38,420 --> 00:18:42,460
Good. Paper stays dry and the toes stay clean.

303
00:18:45,250 --> 00:18:48,410
One squeezed. Three slid. Two felt
comfortable.

304
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:50,840
You explained what you felt.

305
00:18:50,990 --> 00:18:52,830
That helped us choose.

306
00:18:52,980 --> 00:18:58,780
Next time I can tell you before we even look
in the mirror.

307
00:19:00,250 --> 00:19:03,516
My feet will keep their own shoes.

308
00:19:03,666 --> 00:19:05,113
A generous decision.

309
00:19:05,263 --> 00:19:07,620
The small pair thanks you.

310
00:19:07,770 --> 00:19:12,400
Let them know they're safe. These brown ones
are mine.

311
00:19:15,250 --> 00:19:17,530
Next time, a park picnic.

312
00:19:17,680 --> 00:19:19,960
With one clear meeting place.

313
00:19:20,110 --> 00:19:22,830
Can the bench have a name?

314
00:19:22,980 --> 00:19:27,460
We can give it a landmark so we'll know it.

315
00:19:30,250 --> 00:19:33,757
The right shoes needed more listening than
guessing.

316
00:19:33,907 --> 00:19:36,557
And Max told us what mattered.

317
00:19:36,707 --> 00:19:40,214
That is a good fit for this family.

318
00:19:40,364 --> 00:19:44,300
Everybody heard the bit about my heel. That
helped.

319
00:19:45,250 --> 00:19:49,614
My new shoes have a box. Our plan has
directions.

320
00:19:49,764 --> 00:19:52,414
And our team has excellent ears.

321
00:19:52,564 --> 00:19:55,643
Which pair's on your feet right now?

322
00:19:55,793 --> 00:19:59,300
My old green ones. Listen to them squeak!
